stvanpeter-stack","html_url":"https://github.com/kovacsistvanpeter-stack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-24T08:37:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T08:37:29Z","body":"docs-current: no docs change is needed here (see the Docs diff section: authenticated-bots.mdx already describes a restored, signed-in profile; this makes the launch match it). I cannot add labels as an outside contributor, so could a maintainer add `docs: none`? Thanks.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/6382081555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/6583656331","html_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/pull/1873#issuecomment-6583656331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1873","id":6583656331,"node_id":"IC_kwDON109P88AAAABiGqfiw","user":{"login":"igordev23","id":182698900,"node_id":"U_kgDOCuPDlA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182698900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23","html_url":"https://github.com/igordev23","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/igordev23/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-02T17:24:14Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T17:24:14Z","body":"## Validation attestation — #1873 (delivers #1725)\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED.** On a real Google Meet call, an authenticated bot built from this PR's head joins as the signed-in account and transcribes. The stock image fails with `auth_session_missing` on the same deployment, same profile and same meeting. A guest bot on this PR keeps `--incognito` and is admitted normally.\n\nI am a non-author. I found the same root cause independently (see my comment on #1725) and ran this validation myself.\n\n### Setup and build provenance (D12b)\n\n- **Deployment:** full Compose (`make all`) plus the CPU-only transcription stack (`deploy/transcription/docker-compose.cpu.yml` + a local override for 3 CPU workers). Single Linux host, no GPU.\n- **Install:** long-lived, not a fresh clone. The stack was built from `c63ddda` (main); only the bot image changes between runs.\n- **Bot images:**\n  - red control: stock `vexaai/vexa-bot:v012` (`sha256:e2398bfa…`)\n  - green and guest: `vexa/vexa-bot:pr1873`, built locally with `make bot BOT_IMAGE=vexa/vexa-bot:pr1873` from PR head **`bcf9211`** (`sha256:dcb3a24e…`). I confirmed the compiled `dist/capture-bridge.js` contains `inv.authenticated ? getAuthenticatedJoinBrowserArgs() : getJoinBrowserArgs()`.\n- **Env deltas from stock:** `BROWSER_IMAGE` (set per run as above), `BOT_AUTHENTICATED=true` + `BOT_USERDATA_S3_PATH=userdata/bot-identity-1` (`false` for the guest run), transcription pointed at the local CPU workers.\n- **Profile:** one signed-in Google profile, provisioned earlier and restored from the in-stack S3 storage. It was the same profile in every run.\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02, one Meet meeting reused for all three runs, with a human host present and speaking.\n\n### Observations\n\n| Run | Image | Mode | What the bot log shows | Meeting API result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **R1 — red control** (meeting 9) | stock `v012` | authenticated | `Authenticated mode: skipping name input` → `📸 Screenshot: authenticated mode but browser profile is signed out (guest lobby).` | `status: failed`, `completion_reason: auth_session_missing`, `failure_stage: joining` |\n| **G1 — green** (meeting 10) | PR `bcf9211` | authenticated | `Authenticated mode: skipping name input` → `Bot clicked the authenticated join CTA` → `✅ Bot admitted during polling window`. No signed-out message. | `status: completed`, `completion_reason: stopped` (stopped by me after the speech check) |\n| **N1 — guest regression** (meeting 11) | PR `bcf9211` | guest (`BOT_AUTHENTICATED=false`) | name input filled → `Ask to join` → host admitted → `✅ Bot admitted` | `status: completed`, `completion_reason: stopped` |\n\n**Chromium launch args**, read from `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` inside the bot container while it was in the meeting:\n\n- **G1:** 7 Chromium processes on the restored `--user-data-dir`, **none** carrying `--incognito`.\n- **N1:** the browser process carries `--incognito --user-data-dir=…`. So guest launches keep the canonical join set, as the PR intends.\n\n**Transcript (G1):** segments landed through the API during the call, including the host's Portuguese speech: `\"Testando só um, dois, três.\"` One earlier segment was auto-detected as `fr`. That is the known language-detection wobble of the `small` CPU model on short segments, unrelated to this change.\n\n### Rungs not covered\n\n- I validated only the Compose plus CPU-transcription deployment. I did not run Lite, k8s/helm or hosted.\n- I did not run this PR's unit test (`authenticatedArgs.test.ts`) locally; the `node` job is green on the head SHA.\n- I did not test MS Teams or Zoom authenticated launches, or Meet with a second human participant.\n\n### Side note (not a regression of this PR)\n\nOn my host, the G1 teardown hit `aws … ETIMEDOUT` on the auth-profile upload, ending with `Uploaded 0 auth-essential items`. That was my mistake, not the PR's: I restarted the stack (`make all`, which recreates storage) while that bot was still tearing down. No profile files were overwritten, and the R1 teardown on the same profile uploaded 13 items normally.\n\n### Docs (D6c)\n\nI agree with the author that `authenticated-bots.mdx` already describes a restored, signed-in profile. This PR makes the launch match it, so no docs change is needed for this behaviour.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/comments/6583656331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]